Simion departs at time `s` and arrives at time `t = s + ta`. He meets a bus from B if their paths overlap strictly (not at endpoints).

A bus from B departs at time `i` (starting from 05:00 = 300 minutes) and arrives at time `i + tb`. Simion (on road from `s` to `t`) and this bus (on road from `i` to `i+tb`) meet if their intervals overlap strictly.

Two intervals (s, t) and (i, i+tb) overlap strictly if: `s < i + tb` AND `i < t`

That means: the bus departed before Simion arrives, and the bus arrives after Simion departs.

