raw_output:
Looking at the bug, the issue is in the loop bounds. After calling `.Distinct().ToArray()`, the array `m` may have fewer elements than `n`, but the loop uses `n - 1` as the upper bound instead of `m.Length - 1`. This causes an `IndexOutOfRangeException` when accessing `m[i + 1]`.

The fix is to use `m.Length` instead of `n` in the loop condition.

