raw_output:
Looking at the bug, the loop `for(int i=0;;++i)` runs forever because there's no termination condition. The loop should stop when the bus from B departs after the last valid time (end) or when `start + i*b > end`.

The condition for meeting a bus from B that departed at time `start + i*b`:
- It arrives at A at `start + i*b + tb`
- Simion is on the road from `Abegin` to `Aend`
- They meet if `start + i*b < Aend` AND `start + i*b + tb > Abegin`
- Also the bus must depart by `end` (11:59 PM = 23*60+59 = 1439)

The fix is to add a break condition when `start + i*b > end`.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cstdio>
#include <algorithm>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
	int a,ta,b,tb;
	char s[10];
	scanf("%d %d",&a,&ta);
	scanf("%d %d",&b,&tb);
	scanf("%s",s);
	int Abegin = ((s[0]-'0')*10 + s[1]-'0')*60 + 10*(s[3]-'0')+s[4]-'0';
	int Aend = Abegin + ta;
	int start = 300, end = 23*60+59;
	int ans=0;

	for(int i=0; start+i*b <= end; ++i)
	{
		int Bdepart = start + i*b;
		int Barrive = Bdepart + tb;
		// Bus from B departs at Bdepart, arrives at A at Barrive
		// Simion is on road from Abegin to Aend
		// They meet (strictly, not at endpoints) if Bdepart < Aend and Barrive > Abegin
		if(Bdepart < Aend && Barrive > Abegin) ans++;
	}

	printf("%d\n",ans);
	return 0;
}
```

