The buggy code computes Q as F[N][S-R] where N = p-1. F[k][x] is computed as stars-and-bars (number of ways to distribute x among k+1 non-negative integers = C(x+k, k)). So F[N][S-R] = C(S-R+N, N) = C(s-r+p-1, p-1). That seems correct.

